{"format":"rerail.policy/v1","id":"typescript-eslint-no-unused-expressions","revision":6,"mode":"steer","description":"Port of typescript-eslint's `no-unused-expressions` (https://typescript-eslint.io/rules/no-unused-expressions), an extension of ESLint's rule; same document shape as the ESLint port. Flags an expression statement whose expression (through parentheses and TS `as`/`<T>`/`!`/instantiation wrappers) is not a call, `new`, assignment, update, `await`, `yield`, `import()`, `void` or `delete`; directive prologue strings are exempt. tree-sitter reads `e as A.B.C` and `e satisfies A.B.C` (a type name with two or more dots) as a member access on `e as A.B` / `e satisfies A.B`; such a member access is treated as the `as` (unwrapped) or `satisfies` (never flagged, as upstream) it is. A `&&`, `||` or `??` statement whose right operand upstream's `allowShortCircuit` would allow (a call, assignment, `await`, ...) is reported where upstream reports it, under the same code, with upstream's message plus Rerail's: which condition the right operand runs under, to keep it in an `if` (with the rewrite of `a && f()`, `a || f()` or `a ?? f()`); an agent given upstream's message alone dropped the condition. The example is generic because a message cuts a long or multi-line operand. Options are declared in the `options` define (the rule's defaults); a variant is a config patch.","scope":{"include":["**/*.ts","**/*.tsx","**/*.mts","**/*.cts"],"exclude":[]},"clauses":[{"id":"options","define":{"options":{"allowShortCircuit":{"type":"boolean","nullable":true,"default":null},"allowTernary":{"type":"boolean","nullable":true,"default":null}}}},{"id":"shared","define":{"language":"typescript","utils":{"disallowed":{"any":[{"kind":"array"},{"kind":"arrow_function"},{"kind":"class"},{"kind":"function_expression"},{"kind":"generator_function"},{"kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"undefined"},{"kind":"number"},{"kind":"string"},{"kind":"true"},{"kind":"false"},{"kind":"null"},{"kind":"regex"},{"kind":"template_string"},{"kind":"member_expression","not":{"has":{"field":"object","stopBy":"neighbor","any":[{"kind":"as_expression"},{"kind":"satisfies_expression"}]}}},{"kind":"member_expression","has":{"field":"object","stopBy":"neighbor","kind":"as_expression","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","all":[{"not":{"kind":"type_arguments"}},{"matches":"disallowed"}]}}},{"kind":"subscript_expression"},{"kind":"meta_property"},{"kind":"object"},{"kind":"sequence_expression"},{"kind":"this"},{"kind":"super"},{"kind":"unary_expression","not":{"has":{"regex":"^(void|delete)$","stopBy":"neighbor"}}},{"kind":"parenthesized_expression","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","all":[{"not":{"kind":"type_arguments"}},{"matches":"disallowed"}]}},{"kind":"as_expression","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","all":[{"not":{"kind":"type_arguments"}},{"matches":"disallowed"}]}},{"kind":"type_assertion","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","all":[{"not":{"kind":"type_arguments"}},{"matches":"disallowed"}]}},{"kind":"non_null_expression","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","all":[{"not":{"kind":"type_arguments"}},{"matches":"disallowed"}]}},{"kind":"instantiation_expression","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","all":[{"not":{"kind":"type_arguments"}},{"matches":"disallowed"}]}},{"$option":"allowShortCircuit","cases":{"true":[]},"default":[{"kind":"binary_expression"}],"spread":true},{"$option":"allowShortCircuit","cases":{"true":[{"kind":"binary_expression","not":{"has":{"regex":"^(&&|\\|\\||\\?\\?)$","stopBy":"neighbor"}}}]},"default":[],"spread":true},{"$option":"allowShortCircuit","cases":{"true":[{"kind":"binary_expression","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","follows":{"regex":"^(&&|\\|\\||\\?\\?)$","stopBy":"neighbor"},"matches":"disallowed"}}]},"default":[],"spread":true},{"$option":"allowTernary","cases":{"true":[]},"default":[{"kind":"ternary_expression"}],"spread":true},{"$option":"allowTernary","cases":{"true":[{"kind":"ternary_expression","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","matches":"disallowed","follows":{"regex":"^[?:]$","stopBy":"neighbor"}}}]},"default":[],"spread":true},{"kind":"call_expression","has":{"kind":"template_string","stopBy":"neighbor"}}]},"directive-like":{"kind":"expression_statement","has":{"kind":"string","stopBy":"neighbor"}},"directive":{"all":[{"matches":"directive-like"},{"inside":{"stopBy":"neighbor","any":[{"kind":"program"},{"kind":"statement_block","inside":{"stopBy":"neighbor","any":[{"kind":"function_declaration"},{"kind":"function_expression"},{"kind":"arrow_function"},{"kind":"generator_function"},{"kind":"generator_function_declaration"},{"kind":"method_definition"},{"kind":"module"},{"kind":"internal_module"}]}}]}},{"not":{"follows":{"stopBy":"end","all":[{"not":{"kind":"comment"}},{"not":{"kind":"hash_bang_line"}},{"not":{"regex":"^\\{$"}},{"not":{"matches":"directive-like"}}]}}}]},"short-circuit-call":{"kind":"binary_expression","any":[{"pattern":"$_ && $_"},{"pattern":"$_ || $_"},{"pattern":"$_ ?? $_"}],"matches":"disallowed","has":{"field":"right","matches":"runs-under-short-circuit"}},"runs-under-short-circuit":{"any":[{"not":{"matches":"disallowed"}},{"kind":"binary_expression","any":[{"pattern":"$_ && $_"},{"pattern":"$_ || $_"},{"pattern":"$_ ?? $_"}],"has":{"field":"right","matches":"runs-under-short-circuit"}},{"kind":"parenthesized_expression","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","not":{"any":[{"kind":"type_arguments"},{"kind":"comment"},{"regex":"^[()]$"}]},"matches":"runs-under-short-circuit"}}]}}}},{"id":"unused-expression","forbid":{"ast":{"language":"typescript","rule":{"kind":"expression_statement","all":[{"not":{"matches":"directive"}},{"has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","matches":"disallowed","not":{"matches":"short-circuit-call"}}}]}}},"violation":{"anchor":"witness.span","code":"@typescript-eslint/no-unused-expressions","message":"Expected an assignment or function call and instead saw an expression.","suppress":{"eslint":{"rules":["@typescript-eslint/no-unused-expressions"]},"oxlint":{"rules":["no-unused-expressions"]}}}},{"id":"short-circuit-and","forbid":{"ast":{"language":"typescript","rule":{"kind":"expression_statement","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","pattern":"$A && $B","matches":"short-circuit-call"}}}},"violation":{"anchor":"witness.span","code":"@typescript-eslint/no-unused-expressions","message":"Expected an assignment or function call and instead saw an expression. `$B` runs only when `$A` is truthy: keep that condition, moving the call into an `if` as `a && f()` becomes `if (a) { f(); }`.","suppress":{"eslint":{"rules":["@typescript-eslint/no-unused-expressions"]},"oxlint":{"rules":["no-unused-expressions"]}}}},{"id":"short-circuit-or","forbid":{"ast":{"language":"typescript","rule":{"kind":"expression_statement","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","pattern":"$A || $B","matches":"short-circuit-call"}}}},"violation":{"anchor":"witness.span","code":"@typescript-eslint/no-unused-expressions","message":"Expected an assignment or function call and instead saw an expression. `$B` runs only when `$A` is falsy: keep that condition, moving the call into an `if` as `a || f()` becomes `if (!(a)) { f(); }`.","suppress":{"eslint":{"rules":["@typescript-eslint/no-unused-expressions"]},"oxlint":{"rules":["no-unused-expressions"]}}}},{"id":"short-circuit-nullish","forbid":{"ast":{"language":"typescript","rule":{"kind":"expression_statement","has":{"stopBy":"neighbor","pattern":"$A ?? $B","matches":"short-circuit-call"}}}},"violation":{"anchor":"witness.span","code":"@typescript-eslint/no-unused-expressions","message":"Expected an assignment or function call and instead saw an expression. `$B` runs only when `$A` is null or undefined: keep that condition, moving the call into an `if` as `a ?? f()` becomes `if (a === null || a === undefined) { f(); }`.","suppress":{"eslint":{"rules":["@typescript-eslint/no-unused-expressions"]},"oxlint":{"rules":["no-unused-expressions"]}}}}]}
